{"info": {"author": null, "author_email": "Daniel de Kok <daniel@huggingface.co>, David Holtz <david@huggingface.co>", "bugtrack_url": null, "classifiers": [], "description": "# kernels\n\nThe Kernel Hub allows Python libraries and applications to load compute\nkernels directly from the [Hub](https://hf.co/). To support this kind\nof dynamic loading, Hub kernels differ from traditional Python kernel\npackages in that they are made to be:\n\n- Portable: a kernel can be loaded from paths outside `PYTHONPATH`.\n- Unique: multiple versions of the same kernel can be loaded in the\n  same Python process.\n- Compatible: kernels must support all recent versions of Python and\n  the different PyTorch build configurations (various CUDA versions\n  and C++ ABIs). Furthermore, older C library versions must be supported.\n\nThe `kernels` Python package is used to load kernels from the Hub.\n\n## \ud83d\ude80 Quick Start\n\nInstall the `kernels` package with `pip` (requires `torch>=2.5` and CUDA):\n\n```bash\npip install kernels\n```\n\nHere is how you would use the [activation](https://huggingface.co/kernels-community/activation) kernels from the Hugging Face Hub:\n\n```python\nimport torch\n\nfrom kernels import get_kernel\n\n# Download optimized kernels from the Hugging Face hub\nactivation = get_kernel(\"kernels-community/activation\", version=1)\n\n# Random tensor\nx = torch.randn((10, 10), dtype=torch.float16, device=\"cuda\")\n\n# Run the kernel\ny = torch.empty_like(x)\nactivation.gelu_fast(y, x)\n\nprint(y)\n```\n\nYou can [search for kernels](https://huggingface.co/models?other=kernels) on\nthe Hub.\n\n## \ud83d\udcda Documentation\n\nRead the [documentation of kernels](https://huggingface.co/docs/kernels/).\n\n## Test coverage\n\nTo reproduce the coverage number reported on PRs locally:\n\n```bash\nuv run pytest --cov=kernels --cov-report=term-missing tests\n```\n\nCI measures coverage on a single canonical matrix cell (Python 3.10 / Torch 2.12.0) and posts a sticky comment on the PR; the threshold is 80% (warn-only \u2014 the check stays green either way).\n\n", "description_content_type": "text/markdown; charset=UTF-8; variant=GFM", "docs_url": null, "download_url": null, "downloads": {"last_day": -1, "last_month": -1, "last_week": -1}, "dynamic": null, "home_page": "https://github.com/huggingface/kernels", "keywords": null, "license": "Apache-2.0", "license_expression": null, "license_files": null, "maintainer": null, "maintainer_email": null, "name": "kernels", "package_url": "https://pypi.org/project/kernels/", "platform": null, "project_url": "https://pypi.org/project/kernels/", "project_urls": {"Homepage": "https://github.com/huggingface/kernels"}, "provides_extra": ["benchmark", "curated", "curated-xpu", "docs", "sigstore", "torch"], "release_url": "https://pypi.org/project/kernels/0.18.3/", "requires_dist": ["huggingface-hub>=1.32.0", "packaging>=20.0", "pyyaml>=6", "tomli>=2.0; python_full_version < \"3.11\"", "typing-extensions>=4.0; python_full_version < \"3.11\"", "tomlkit>=0.13.3", "matplotlib>=3.7.0; extra == \"benchmark\"", "numpy>=2.0.2; extra == \"benchmark\"", "tabulate>=0.9.0; extra == \"benchmark\"", "torch; extra == \"benchmark\"", "nvidia-cutlass-dsl; extra == \"curated\"", "einops; extra == \"curated\"", "apache-tvm-ffi<0.2.0,>=0.1.9; extra == \"curated\"", "einops; extra == \"curated-xpu\"", "apache-tvm-ffi<0.2.0,>=0.1.9; extra == \"curated-xpu\"", "hf-doc-builder; extra == \"docs\"", "sigstore<5,>=4; extra == \"sigstore\"", "torch; extra == \"torch\""], "requires_python": ">=3.10", "summary": "Download compute kernels", "version": "0.18.3", "yanked": false, "yanked_reason": null}, "release_dates": {"0.1.7": "2025-02-25T16:13:24.661529Z", "0.10.0": "2025-09-05T08:54:13.043839Z", "0.10.1": "2025-09-10T07:43:17.927113Z", "0.10.2": "2025-09-22T18:15:47.456905Z", "0.10.3": "2025-10-13T15:26:09.467258Z", "0.10.4": "2025-10-16T18:24:23.004477Z", "0.10.5": "2025-12-04T09:14:24.421970Z", "0.11.0": "2025-10-31T10: